IMPORT prelude

§ `Fact vocabulary (from schema.md, verbatim)`

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF Sickness, `Accidental injury`, Neither

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
  Skydiving, `Military service`, Firefighting, `Police service`, Other

DECLARE Claim
  HAS `agreement signed`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `premium paid month`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hospitalization month`                      IS A NUMBER
      `hospitalization ground`                     IS A Ground
      `age at hospitalization`                     IS A NUMBER
      `causes`                                     IS A LIST OF Cause
      `fraud month`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `misrepresentation month`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit month`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `written confirmation month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `dispute arisen`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to settle month`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `arbitration commenced month`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `valid arbitration award issued`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `written proof of claim month`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `recovery sought month`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `policy term months`                         IS A NUMBER

GIVEN  `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
       `limit month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no later than` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m AT MOST `limit month`

GIVEN  cs IS A LIST OF Cause
       c  IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arose out of` MEANS elem c cs

§ `Section 1 -- Policy In Effect And Conditions`

§§ `1.3 -- Timely wellness visit and written confirmation`

-- 1.3 has two deadlines: the wellness visit itself no later than the 6th month
-- anniversary (with a qualified provider), and the written confirmation of it no
-- later than the 7th month anniversary. Per 1.1(3), the policy stays in effect while
-- 1.3 is "still pending" -- i.e. as of the hospitalization, the relevant deadline has
-- simply not yet arrived -- as an alternative to already having been satisfied. Each
-- sub-part is therefore "timely, or not yet due", evaluated as of the month of
-- hospitalization, consistent with 1.1's own framing ("in effect AT THE TIME OF the
-- hospitalization").

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness visit is timely or not yet due` claim MEANS
        (`no later than` (claim's `wellness visit month`) 6 AND claim's `wellness visit provider qualified`)
    OR  claim's `hospitalization month` AT MOST 6

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`written confirmation is timely or not yet due` claim MEANS
        `no later than` (claim's `written confirmation month`) 7
    OR  claim's `hospitalization month` AT MOST 7

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`condition 1.3 satisfied or still pending` claim MEANS
        `wellness visit is timely or not yet due` claim
    AND `written confirmation is timely or not yet due` claim

§§ `1.2 -- Cancelation`

-- "misrepresentation" below also stands in for "material withholding of any
-- information", which 1.2 names as a further, distinct ground for cancelation, but
-- for which the schema provides no separate field. See NOTES.md.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fraud or misrepresentation by the time of hospitalization` claim MEANS
        `no later than` (claim's `fraud month`) (claim's `hospitalization month`)
    OR  `no later than` (claim's `misrepresentation month`) (claim's `hospitalization month`)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy term has ended by the time of hospitalization` claim MEANS
    claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN claim's `policy term months`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy canceled` claim MEANS
        `fraud or misrepresentation by the time of hospitalization` claim
    OR  NOT (`condition 1.3 satisfied or still pending` claim)
    OR  `policy term has ended by the time of hospitalization` claim

§§ `1.1 -- Policy in effect`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy in effect at the time of hospitalization` claim MEANS
        claim's `agreement signed`
    AND isJust (claim's `premium paid month`)
    AND `condition 1.3 satisfied or still pending` claim
    AND NOT (`policy canceled` claim)

§§ `1.1 -- Hospitalization for a covered ground`

-- 1.1 conditions payment on "hospitalization for sickness or accidental injury";
-- Neither is not a covered ground at all.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `hospitalization ground`
    WHEN Sickness            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Accidental injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN Neither             THEN FALSE

§ `Section 2 -- General Exclusions`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`event arose out of an excluded activity` claim MEANS
        `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Skydiving
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Military service`
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Firefighting
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Police service`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`excluded by age` claim MEANS
    claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a general exclusion applies` claim MEANS
        `event arose out of an excluded activity` claim
    OR  `excluded by age` claim

§ `Section 3 -- General Conditions`

§§ `3.2 -- Arbitration`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration commenced within three months of impasse` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `unable to settle month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST u  THEN `no later than` (claim's `arbitration commenced month`) (u PLUS 3)

-- Where a dispute has arisen, timely arbitration and a valid award are conditions
-- precedent to liability; where none has arisen the whole clause is vacuous.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration precondition satisfied` claim MEANS
    NOT claim's `dispute arisen`
    OR  (    `arbitration commenced within three months of impasse` claim
         AND claim's `valid arbitration award issued`)

-- "sixty (60) days" is read as two months, consistent with the month-level
-- granularity used throughout the rest of the schema; see NOTES.md.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sixty day waiting period observed` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `recovery sought month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST r  THEN
        CONSIDER claim's `written proof of claim month`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST p  THEN r AT LEAST (p PLUS 2)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3.2 conditions satisfied` claim MEANS
        `arbitration precondition satisfied` claim
    AND `sixty day waiting period observed` claim

§ `Coverage decision`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
covered claim MEANS
        `policy in effect at the time of hospitalization` claim
    AND `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury` claim
    AND NOT (`a general exclusion applies` claim)
    AND `section 3.2 conditions satisfied` claim
